{
  "requirement": "TBV owns the model conversation, supported backend integrations, tool\ndispatch, and structured submission used by its ask builder.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "structural: The only structural obligation is the clause \"TBV owns the model conversation, supported backend integrations, tool dispatch, and structured submission used by its ask builder.\" A version that handed these to an external agent framework would produce the same results but would violate that clause. The rest of the text describes behaviour only.\n\nThe two roots cover it:\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#impl[ToolAgent<P, T>]#2/fn[run_with_domain_tools]` builds the opening `CompletionRequest`, wraps the `ToolFactory` session in `SessionTools`, and creates a `GraphSession`. It then drives TBV's own `converse` loop in `agent.rs` over a generic `CompletionProvider`. TBV's `Conversation` implementation for `GraphSession` carries the tool definitions, `dispatch` and `submit`, with `submission_tool` and `submitted_value` alongside. The call chain reaches all of this from the marked root, so those items need no markers of their own.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/providers.rs#impl[RigProvider]/fn[connect]` owns the backend integrations. It maps `BackendConfig` onto the Bedrock, OpenAI and Ollama completion models and erases them behind TBV's `RigProvider`.\n\nI found no gap and no further root is needed.\n\nbehavioral: `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.tool_agent` is an umbrella statement. TBV owns four things: the model conversation, the supported backend integrations, tool dispatch, and structured submission. The detailed obligations sit in refining requirements (`isolation`, `submission`, `submission.mcp`, `fixed_tools`, the per-backend configs, and `provider_failure`), which are assessed separately. I checked each of the four owned areas against the marked tests. The supported backends are Bedrock, OpenAI and Ollama, per `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#enum[AgentConfig]`.\n\n- **Model conversation and backend integration, OpenAI.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_openai_backend_runs_independent_calls_against_a_local_transport]` runs two full conversations against a local transport. It asserts the model, the token limit, and the exact tool list. It asserts the `submit_result` schema, the prompt contents, and the finishing instruction. On the second turn it asserts that the tool output (\"a source snapshot\") appears in the replayed history, and on the first turn that it does not. It also asserts that the answer is returned with its dependencies.\n- **Backend integration, Ollama.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[supplied_ollama_backend_delivers_tools_and_results_over_native_chat]` checks the native `/api/chat` POST and the bearer authorization. It checks the options, the `submit_result` schema, and that the tool result is delivered as a `tool` message on turn 1. It also checks that the submitted answer is returned.\n- **Backend integration, Bedrock.** Bedrock needs AWS services, so an end-to-end conversation would depend on the network. The Bedrock-specific behavior is instead tested locally:\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[typed_client_calls_preserve_order_and_native_history]` checks that tool calls are normalized with order and native history preserved.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[cache_checkpoints_are_requested_for_caching_models]` checks cache checkpoints.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/providers.rs#mod[tests]/fn[bedrock_native_option_types_are_checked_and_only_max_tokens_is_defaulted]` checks option handling.\n- **Tool dispatch.** The OpenAI and Ollama tests dispatch `read_node` and feed its result back into the conversation. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[application_tool_factories_create_fresh_state_for_each_agent_call]` dispatches application tools (`increment`). It asserts the results reach the next request, that tool state is fresh for each call, and that the tool is advertised in the request.\n- **Structured submission.** Both backend tests submit via `submit_result` and assert the typed answer. The OpenAI and Ollama tests also assert the submit schema (`required: [\"result\"]`).\n- **Concurrent conversation ownership.** The `ParallelConversations` provider in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` is cited only as a helper. The `isolation` refinement carries this obligation, and it needs no separate test here.\n\nI found no behavioral obligation in this text that lacks a test, and no marking gap.",
  "references": "62926707a5cf8176cc0c62915480ec91fbc0a4bbb8b25120683f033471116613",
